      "title": "Nonlinear model predictive control of legged robots with accelerated first-order optimization",
      "takeaway": "This method paper addresses nonlinearly constrained, nonconvex MPC for legged robots by proposing a nonmonotone Accelerated Projected Gradient (APG) algorithm with Nesterov momentum and backtracking line search, which uses only gradient information and closed-form projections to handle friction-cone and box constraints without Hessian or constraint-derivative computations. Against a Sequential Quadratic Programming (SQP) baseline, the abstract reports shorter computation times and lower objective values in the considered test scenarios, with improved tracking performance, and states that the low per-iteration cost enables real-time nonlinear MPC at 100 Hz on an embedded single-board computer. Evidence comes from offline comparisons, real-time simulations, and experiments on a quadruped robot plus biped simulations. Inspect how the nonmonotone APG and line search are configured, how constraints are projected, and how the SQP comparison and embedded timing were set up.",
